GPT-4 LAB – 30 COMPLETE STANDALONE PROGRAMS
Every question below has a complete independent Python program. Each program includes the reusable Ollama connection, display function, and save function where needed. You can run each question separately.
Common setup (do this once)
•	Install the requests package: pip install requests
•	Download the model: ollama pull llama3.2
•	Keep Ollama running while executing the Python program.
•	Save the required question code as a .py file and run it in VS Code.
•	For Questions 7 and 27, create resume.txt in the same folder and paste resume content into it.
•	The FAQ data in Questions 8 and 28 is sample data; replace it with the actual FAQ dataset if your question supplies one.
 
Question 1: Grammar Correction Assistant
import requests

# Reusable function to connect Python with Ollama
def ask_ollama(prompt):
    url = "http://localhost:11434/api/generate"
    data = {
        "model": "llama3.2",
        "prompt": prompt,
        "stream": False
    }
    response = requests.post(url, json=data)
    response.raise_for_status()
    return response.json()["response"]

# Reusable function to display the AI response
def display_result(result):
    print("\n----- AI OUTPUT -----\n")
    print(result)

# Reusable function to save the AI response in a text file
def save_result(result, filename):
    with open(filename, "w", encoding="utf-8") as file:
        file.write(result)
    print("\nResult saved in", filename)


text = input("Enter a sentence or paragraph: ")
prompt = f"""Correct grammatical and spelling errors in the text.
Preserve the original meaning. Return the corrected text.

Text: {text}"""
result = ask_ollama(prompt)
display_result(result)
save_result(result, "corrected_text.txt")

 
